"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"definitions\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The source does not define every benefit as a gift. Unit u13 says returns or incentives may be gifts; u8 describes only typical guaranteed-return components. Gift classification and whether a rebate is genuinely a fee or charge discount require judgment.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u8\\\",\\\"u13\\\",\\\"u14\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The parenthetical discount exception attaches to gifts in u14. Its later reference to gifts being bound by this requirement most naturally incorporates that exception. A hypothesis that product-type linkage cancels the exception lacks affirmative textual support and is not retained. Section 103 authorization or exemption in u10 does not supply an exception to paragraph 3.11. Mixed-package classification remains unresolved.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u10\\\",\\\"u13\\\",\\\"u14\\\",\\\"u15\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"modality\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The selected restriction uses should not; it is presented as a regulatory requirement, without establishing statutory offence liability. The possible gift and structured-product classifications retain their may qualifications. Actual distraction is explanatory, not an additional express trigger. Separate provisions use offence, must, best endeavours and discretionary may language.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u10\\\",\\\"u13\\\",\\\"u14\\\",\\\"u19\\\",\\\"u21\\\",\\\"u24\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"time\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The supplied text establishes no effective date or transition rule for this control. The 30 September 2010 date identifies the FAQ, not commencement. Monitoring language and guidance issued from time to time do not identify applicable versions.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u24\\\",\\\"u30\\\",\\\"u31\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"dependencies\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The external-authorities.23ec46 dependency is missing. Full paragraph 3.11 and the cited FAQ are material to scope and exception classification. Section 103, paragraph 2.3, General Principle 1, disclosure principles and advertising guidance govern separate issues that the selected Boolean control cannot resolve.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u10\\\",\\\"u12\\\",\\\"u18\\\",\\\"u21\\\",\\\"u22\\\",\\\"u28\\\",\\\"u29\\\",\\\"u30\\\",\\\"u31\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Does the complete paragraph 3.11 support applying this circular’s quoted gift control to other investment products promoted by its defined distributors?\\\",\\n    \\\"How do paragraph 3.11 and the cited FAQ classify conditional rebates, third-party fee discounts, and mixed packages of discounts and other benefits?\\\",\\n    \\\"Which versions and effective dates of the cited authorities govern the assessed offer?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"readings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Assess one identified offer or proposed offer to a client.\\\",\\n        \\\"The circular’s distributor category supplies actor scope; u14 supplies broader investment-product scope.\\\",\\n        \\\"The discount exception applies to both specific-product and product-type promotions.\\\",\\n        \\\"For the offer-level screen, each gift component is assessed separately; any non-discount gift prevents a pass.\\\",\\n        \\\"A true result is a selected paragraph-10 gift-control pass only when scope is true. It establishes neither overall compliance nor legal correctness.\\\",\\n        \\\"Unknown facts remain unknown.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\": [\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u1\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u14\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"then such gifts will be bound by this requirement\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u14\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Even where the guaranteed returns offered would not constitute a “structured product” under the SFO\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u13\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"unless the SFC has authorised the issue or an exemption applies.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u10\\\"}\\n      ],\\n      \\\"distinction\\\":\\\"Retains the parent’s broader product scope and the discount exception throughout u14. The exception-attachment investigation does not support removing the exception for product-type-linked gifts or importing section 103 exemptions into this control. In the supplied probe, this reading has true scope and a true selected result; the unknown fund-promotion fact is irrelevant here. The strongest uncertainty is the broader scope without the complete Code provision.\\\",\\n      \\\"family\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\n      \\\"formalization\\\": {\\n        \\\"facts\\\": [\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds within the circular’s distributor category.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"is_distributor\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed activity promotes a specific investment product or particular investment-product type to a client, including a substantively linked gift arrangement of the kind described in u14.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"has_product_promotion_link\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u14\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed promotion concerns SFC-authorised funds.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"promotes_authorised_funds\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u13\\\",\\\"u15\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed offer includes a benefit classified as a gift for the selected control, before applying the discount exception.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"offers_gift\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u13\\\",\\\"u14\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"},\\n          {\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"Every gift component in the assessed offer qualifies as a discount of fees or charges; any non-discount gift component makes this false.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"all_gifts_are_fee_discounts\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u14\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"}\\n        ],\\n        \\\"result\\\":\\\"(or (not offers_gift) all_gifts_are_fee_discounts)\\\",\\n        \\\"result_type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n        \\\"scope\\\":\\\"(and is_distributor has_product_promotion_link)\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"local_id\\\":\\\"r1\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Does the full Code provision confirm the broader product scope?\\\",\\n        \\\"Does authoritative guidance support the assumed component-by-component treatment of mixed offers?\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"statement\\\":\\\"For the circular’s defined distributors, read u14 as a gift control covering promotion of any specific investment product or product type. The fee-or-charge discount exception remains available when the gift is linked to a product type. Neither absence of structured-product status nor section 103 authorization independently excuses a non-discount gift under this selected control.\\\",\\n      \\\"subject\\\":\\\"Selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control: broad product scope with retained discount exception\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Assess one identified offer or proposed offer to a client.\\\",\\n        \\\"The circular’s fund-focused context limits this selected application to SFC-authorised-fund promotions, without determining the Code’s wider reach.\\\",\\n        \\\"The discount exception applies to both specific-product and product-type promotions.\\\",\\n        \\\"For the offer-level screen, each gift component is assessed separately; any non-discount gift prevents a pass.\\\",\\n        \\\"A true result is a selected paragraph-10 gift-control pass only when scope is true. It establishes neither overall compliance nor legal correctness.\\\",\\n        \\\"Unknown facts remain unknown.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\": [\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"This circular summarises the Securities and Futures Commission’s (SFC) recent observations of licensed corporations’ practices in offering and promoting SFC-authorised funds.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u1\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"in offering such returns or other incentives in promoting SFC-authorised funds\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u13\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u14\\\"},\\n        {\\\"quote\\\":\\\"when offering or promoting funds, distributors should not offer additional returns (which are not part of the product features set out in the relevant offering documents) or other incentives to investors in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u15\\\"}\\n      ],\\n      \\\"distinctio