and is_distributor has_product_promotion_link)"},"local_id":"r1","questions":["Does the full Code provision confirm the broader product scope?","Does authoritative guidance support the assumed component-by-component treatment of mixed offers?"],"statement":"For the circular’s defined distributors, read u14 as a gift control covering promotion of any specific investment product or product type. The fee-or-charge discount exception remains available when the gift is linked to a product type. Neither absence of structured-product status nor section 103 authorization independently excuses a non-discount gift under this selected control.","subject":"Selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control: broad product scope with retained discount exception"},{"assumptions":["Assess one identified offer or proposed offer to a client.","The circular’s fund-focused context limits this selected application to SFC-authorised-fund promotions, without determining the Code’s wider reach.","The discount exception applies to both specific-product and product-type promotions.","For the offer-level screen, each gift component is assessed separately; any non-discount gift prevents a pass.","A true result is a selected paragraph-10 gift-control pass only when scope is true. It establishes neither overall compliance nor legal correctness.","Unknown facts remain unknown."],"citations":[{"quote":"This circular summarises the Securities and Futures Commission’s (SFC) recent observations of licensed corporations’ practices in offering and promoting SFC-authorised funds.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"in offering such returns or other incentives in promoting SFC-authorised funds","unit_id":"u13"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"when offering or promoting funds, distributors should not offer additional returns (which are not part of the product features set out in the relevant offering documents) or other incentives to investors in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct.","unit_id":"u15"}],"distinction":"This rival changes only product scope, not exception attachment or fact meanings. A promotion outside SFC-authorised funds falls outside this selected application. In the supplied probe its scope remains unknown, although its result expression is true; this is not a finding that the gift fails. The incomparable-binding diagnostics do not establish substantive disagreement. The strongest uncertainty is whether u14’s general wording defeats the contextual limitation.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds within the circular’s distributor category.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed activity promotes a specific investment product or particular investment-product type to a client, including a substantively linked gift arrangement of the kind described in u14.","name":"has_product_promotion_link","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed promotion concerns SFC-authorised funds.","name":"promotes_authorised_funds","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u15"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed offer includes a benefit classified as a gift for the selected control, before applying the discount exception.","name":"offers_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Every gift component in the assessed offer qualifies as a discount of fees or charges; any non-discount gift component makes this false.","name":"all_gifts_are_fee_discounts","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(or (not offers_gift) all_gifts_are_fee_discounts)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor promotes_authorised_funds has_product_promotion_link)"},"local_id":"r2","questions":["Is u14 stating a broader operative rule here or explaining its application within the circular’s fund-specific subject?","What evidence establishes whether the assessed promotion concerns SFC-authorised funds?"],"statement":"Read the circular’s selected gift control as applying to SFC-authorised-fund promotions by its defined distributors. Within that scope, retain the fee-or-charge discount exception for both specific-fund and fund-type linkage; do not treat this limitation as an exemption from the Code’s possible wider requirements.","subject":"Selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control: fund-specific application with retained discount exception"}]}},"run_id":"run.43cfe1f6c26f47b89fa28eb53ba97027"}